-- | The courier's portrait for the talk box, pixel by pixel: 118 by 154, from the
-- character sheet, at its own pixel grid. Generated by tools/make-portrait.py; edit
-- the patches here by hand if her face changes.
-- This module exports data only: no animation, bitmap conversion or IO happens
-- here. TalkBox turns the palette and rows into one cached RGBA bitmap, then
-- draws the three patches over it for blinking and speaking. Width and height
-- are source pixels; TalkBox normally scales one pixel to three canvas units.
-- The palette is 0xRRGGBB, while transparency comes from an absent palette key.
-- Patch coordinates use the same top-left origin as the rows (x right, y down).
